      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Learn the drug development process before interviewing.</strong> Any non-scientific business role in biotech (BD, program management, regulatory, market access) requires fluency in the drug development lifecycle. Candidates who cannot discuss Phase I–III clinical trials, FDA regulatory submissions, and IND/NDA processes are not competitive for Boston biotech business roles.</li>
        <li><strong>MassBio events are the primary networking venue.</strong> The Massachusetts Biotechnology Council (MassBio) runs frequent events and conferences that attract the Boston biotech community. Attendance and active participation in MassBio events is the highest-ROI networking activity for Boston biotech job seekers.</li>
        <li><strong>Kendall Square is a walkable community.</strong> The physical density of biotech companies in Kendall Square means that personal relationships develop through proximity. If you're targeting Kendall Square biotech roles, being physically present — at events, at shared coffee shops, at community programming — accelerates network building.</li>
        <li><strong>Model pre-IPO stock options carefully.</strong> Boston biotech companies frequently offer stock options at pre-IPO companies. Understand the strike price, last 409A, vesting schedule, and change-of-control provisions before comparing the total package to other offers.</li>
